//? Title: Spatial Transformers: Tensor Warps and Explicit Paired MNIST Fits
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A localization network predicts where an affine grid samples an image. We verify sampling
values and all affine derivatives, generate distorted MNIST entirely with tensors, then show
every Adam update of full classifiers with and without a learned transformer.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.5_attention_and_modern_convnets/spatial_transformer.cpp`.

> The method

Theta is a row-major 2×3 OUTPUT-TO-INPUT affine map. Coordinates run from −1 to1 at the
outer pixel centres (align_corners=true); bilinear samples outside the image read zero.
A positive x translation therefore samples farther right and moves visible content LEFT.
A 9×9 fixture checks identity, a one-pixel translation and a quarter turn against pixel values.
All six derivatives of a generic fractional map agree with Float64 central differences.
At exact integer pixel coordinates the core sampler uses symmetric one-sided slopes; the
legacy floor-gather implementation could pick one side by roundoff. Learned identity starts
are therefore value-compatible but need not have identical derivative trajectories.

Localization uses 5×5/20/ReLU/SAME-pool, another 5×5/20/ReLU/pool, dense 50/ReLU and dense 6.
The final head has zero weights and bias (1,0,0,0,1,0), so its initial theta is identity.
Sampling agrees within coordinate roundoff. At42 pixels it has 131896 parameters. The zero
head initially blocks gradients to earlier localization filters; head updates can activate
those paths. There is no BN/dropout or bound on theta. A transform can zoom/crop off canvas,
where blank sampling can lose informative gradients; the fit reports its selected blank fraction.

The data factory replaces the source's HOST preprocessing with tensor arithmetic. It draws
angles within±45 degrees, scales .7–1.2 and centre translations within room computed from
14*scale*(abs(cos)+abs(sin)) on a 42-pixel canvas. It forms inverse normalized coordinates,
bilinearly samples, rounds positive pixel values with floor(255*x+.5), clamps0..255 and divides255.
Very large rotated squares may still crop. This detached dataset generation is separate from
the differentiable learned transformer. Tensor RNG draws preserve ranges/distributions but
differ from the source's interleaved std::mt19937_64 sequence; bitwise-identical distorted
images are not claimed. Development/test use independent seeds 101/202.

Both models use the full source CNN: biased He-uniform 5×5/32/ReLU/pool,5×5/64/ReLU/pool,
Glorot dense 128/ReLU and ten logits. Ceiling pools give11×11×64 features. Baseline learns
1044746 scalars; adding localization gives 1176642. Architecture-order initialization consumes
different random draws, so equal seeds do not imply identical classifier weights. All model
computation, affine coefficients, preprocessing, losses and updates use the tensor library.

The visible paired fits use 128 fit/64 validation/64 official-test digits and 6 batch-eight
epochs of Adam(.001) (kept short so both fits run in seconds), explicit kernel L2=.0001/2 and no further augmentation. The same fixed
distorted cohorts enter both models. Validation selects parameters separately; no moving BN
state exists. The final gallery reloads the selected STN and shows actual test warps without
supervised geometric inversion. These bounded single-seed fits cannot establish benchmark
superiority, reproduce the source's much larger schedule or guarantee recovery of the true pose.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/spatial_transformer_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/spatial_transformer_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/spatial_transformer_concept.tikz > build/spatial_transformer_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/spatial_transformer_concept.svg build/spatial_transformer_concept.dvi > build/spatial_transformer_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
