Transformer=true: 1176642 learned scalars, 96 explicit Adam updates; selected epoch 2, validation NLL 2.250255, inference fit NLL 1.151433, test NLL 2.245193, test accuracy 0.312500.
Selected STN fraction of64 test images with mean absolute warped intensity <=1e-5: 0.000000.
\image(figures/spatial_transformer_training.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Both full CNNs use identical fixed distorted cohorts and explicit 6-epoch batch-eight Adam loops with kernel L2. Baseline and transformer have separate validation-selected parameter checkpoints. No BN state or extra augmentation is present. The two count matrices use the 64 official-test images; the data generator’s test seed is independent.)
\alttext(Both full CNNs use identical fixed distorted cohorts and explicit 6-epoch batch-eight Adam loops with kernel L2. Baseline and transformer have separate validation-selected parameter checkpoints. No BN state or extra augmentation is present. The two count matrices use the 64 official-test images; the data generator’s test seed is independent.)

> Selected learned sampling

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/spatial_transformer_learned.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::set_num_threads(2);

  std::filesystem::path cache;
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR"))
    cache = p;
  else if (const auto *p = std::getenv("XDG_CACHE_HOME"))
    cache = std::filesystem::path(p) / "datamunge/datasets";
  else
    cache = std::filesystem::path(std::getenv("HOME")) / ".cache/datamunge/datasets";
  dm::datasets::fetch("mnist", (cache / "mnist").string());

  const auto data = n::load_mnist((cache / "mnist").string(), "test");
  n::Generator generator(202);
  const auto distorted =
      n::models::DistortMnist(n::slice_axis(data.images, 0, 0, 64), generator).images;
  std::vector<int64_t> rows;
  for (int digit = 0; digit < 10; ++digit) {
    bool found = false;
    for (int row = 0; row < 64; ++row)
      if (data.labels.at({row}) == digit) {
        rows.push_back(row);
        found = true;
        break;
      }
    if (!found)
      return 1;
  }
  n::NoGradGuard guard;
  n::ParameterStore p(17);
  n::models::StnMnistClassifier(p, n::zeros({1, 42, 42, 1}), true);
  p.load("build/spatial_transformer_stn_best.npz");
  const auto selected = n::take_rows(distorted, rows);
  const auto out = n::models::StnMnistClassifier(p, selected, true);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  n::save_image_grid(n::concat({selected, out.transformed}, 0),
                     "build/spatial_transformer_learned.png", 5, 0., 1., 4, 1., 3);
  std::print(
      "Top two rows: distorted official-test examples in class order0-9. Bottom two rows: the "
      "same inputs warped by the selected STN checkpoint. Affine coefficients are "
      "unconstrained; this is observed sampling, not supervised geometric recovery.\n");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Top two rows: distorted official-test examples in class order0-9. Bottom two rows: the same inputs warped by the selected STN checkpoint. Affine coefficients are unconstrained; this is observed sampling, not supervised geometric recovery.
\image(figures/spatial_transformer_learned.png)
// result_end
\caption(The selected transformer acts on the same ten official-test inputs shown in the top two rows. The bottom two rows show its actual learned warps in the same order. Geometric transforms were not supervised or forced to invert the known data-generation matrices; blank or cropped outputs, if present, remain visible.)
\alttext(The selected transformer acts on the same ten official-test inputs shown in the top two rows. The bottom two rows show its actual learned warps in the same order. Geometric transforms were not supervised or forced to invert the known data-generation matrices; blank or cropped outputs, if present, remain visible.)


> Observed paired result

Baseline validation selects epoch 1: validation NLL 2.234509, inference fit NLL
1.819659, test NLL 2.162720 and 15/64 correct predictions (23.4375%). STN validation
selects epoch 2: validation NLL 2.250255, inference fit NLL 1.151433, test NLL
2.245193 and 20/64 correct predictions (31.25%). Both curves then overfit this
small cohort. The selected STN has zero test images below the stated blank-intensity
threshold; its shown warps remain close to the distorted inputs. Independent
initializations and 64 test digits do not support a reliable architecture ranking.

> Native confusion matrices

These matrices use the held-out predictions from the executed program above.
The native `ConfusionMatrix` SVG API labels exact counts with true classes
running from top to bottom and predicted classes from left to right.

\image(figures/spatial_transformer_confusion_api_0.svg)
\caption(Held-out classification confusion counts, evaluation 1. Exact cell counts are printed in the image.)
\alttext(Integer prediction counts with true classes as rows and predicted classes as columns.)

\image(figures/spatial_transformer_confusion_api_1.svg)
\caption(Held-out classification confusion counts, evaluation 2. Exact cell counts are printed in the image.)
\alttext(Integer prediction counts with true classes as rows and predicted classes as columns.)


> Conclusion

Tensor sampling exposes mapping direction, boundary behavior and localization gradients.
A tensor-only distortion generator and visible paired optimization connect the full models to
real digits. Actual selected warps and held-out metrics remain distinct from supervised pose
recovery and published accuracy claims.

> References

- [Jaderberg et al. (2015), Spatial Transformer Networks](https://arxiv.org/abs/1506.02025).
- [MNIST dataset](https://yann.lecun.org/exdb/mnist/).
